    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **54 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level-computation rule with a points system, mapping points to a level and returning both fields.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a new `membershipPoints` field (int, min 0) and updated `membershipLevel` to describe it as derived from points (max raised from 3 to 4).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added the `membershipPoints` mapping and split the logic into two methods:\n   - `membershipPoints(owner)`: starts at 0; `+2` email present, `+1` `namesakeCount == 0`, `+2` `householdMemberCount >= 3`, `+3` tenure over 365 days.\n   - `membershipLevel(owner)`: maps points \u2192 level (1 for 0\u20131, 2 for 2\u20133, 3 for 4\u20135, 4 for 6+).\n\nThe \"household of 3 or more\" factor reads the existing `householdMemberCount` (set by `AssignHouseholdMemberCount`), and the tenure factor keeps using `registrationDate`. Since a newly created owner has zero tenure, the maximum a new owner can reach is 5 points \u2192 level 3, matching the Cp39 \"never 4\" test.\n\nVerified all new membership tests (Cp15, Cp23, Cp24, Cp39, Cp40) and the full suite pass.",
