    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered pipeline for `POST /api/owners` (`owners.POST.yml`). Every step runs under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the whole request commits once at the end. Validations reject before any write; side-effects mutate the owner in place and are read by later steps.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 the file's `composition.authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"` requires the caller to hold `OWNER_ADMIN`; otherwise the pipeline never runs.\n\n## 1. `ValidateOwnerFields` (reads the `@RequestBody` \u2014 the only step that does)\nValidations:\n- **Required fields** \u2014 `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone` must be non-null and non-blank; `address` must be non-blank *after normalization*. All offending fields are collected and returned together \u2192 **400** (`OwnerFieldsInvalidException`).\n- **registrationDate not in the future** \u2014 a supplied date later than `LocalDate.now()` \u2192 400. Absent is allowed.\n- **Telephone must form valid E.164** \u2014 normalized via `E164Telephone`; `null` result \u2192 400.\n- **Email (optional) syntactic check** \u2014 must match the email regex \u2192 400 if present-and-malformed.\n- **Email disposable-domain block** \u2014 `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com` \u2192 400. *(Not mentioned in the YAML comments.)*\n\nSide-effects (written back onto the DTO body, published for later steps):\n- Address normalized (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST`/`RD`/`AVE`) and stored back.\n- Telephone rewritten to E.164 form.\n- Email trimmed + lower-cased and stored back (only when present).\n\n## 2. `ValidatePostcode`\n- If postcode **absent/blank** \u2192 accepted, no change.\n- If present: must be **exactly 4 digits** \u2192 else 400.\n- If the city maps to a known region (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`), postcode must fall in that region's inclusive range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 else 400. Unknown city accepts any 4-digit value.\n\n## 3. `CheckOwnerCityCapacity`\n- Rejects with **409** if the owner's city (case-insensitive) already contains **\u2265 50** owners.\n\n## 4. `CheckOwnerDailyCreateLimit`\n- Rejects with **429** if **\u2265 100** owners already have a `registrationDate` equal to today's business day (today rolled forward off weekends via `BusinessDays.rollForward`).\n\n## 5. `BuildOwner` (side-effects \u2014 DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity)\n- Maps the DTO to an `Owner` via `OwnerMapper`.\n- Defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when none supplied.\n- Rolls `registrationDate` forward off weekends to the next business day.\n\n## 6. `AssignHouseholdId` (side-effect)\n- Sets `householdId` = first 12 hex of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode)` (lower-case/trimmed/whitespace-collapsed last name; absent postcode \u2192 empty string). Deterministic \u2014 shared by same last name + postcode.\n\n## 7. `CheckHouseholdUnique`\n- Rejects with **409** if the computed `householdId` already belongs to an existing owner \u2014 **unless** the request declared `sharesHousehold: true`, which bypasses this block only.\n\n## 8. `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`\n- Rejects with **409** if the owner's full `identityKey` = `normalizedTelephone|email|householdId` (from `OwnerIdentityKey`) exactly matches an existing owner's. (Same household with a different phone \u2192 different key \u2192 allowed.)\n\n## 9. `AssignHouseholdMemberCount` (side-effect)\n- Sets `householdMemberCount` = existing owners sharing the `householdId` **+ 1** (the new, not-yet-saved owner).\n\n## 10. `AssignNamesakeCount` (side-effect)\n- Sets `namesakeCount` = count of existing owners sharing this owner's `firstName` + `lastName` (case-insensitive), excluding the new one.\n\n## 11. `AssignCustomerCode` (side-effect)\n- Sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, where REGION comes from the postcode (`OwnerRegion`) and HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`. Does not read the repository.\n\n## 12. `AssignBulkSignupWarning` (side-effect)\n- Sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` when **> 80** owners were already created on today's business day, else `false`.\n\n## 13. `AssignPossibleDuplicate` (side-effect)\n- Soft-match: sets `possibleDuplicate = true` and `possibleDuplicateOf =` the lowest-id matching owner when an existing owner shares this owner's `lastName` (case-insensitive) + exact `postcode` but has a **different** normalized telephone and a **different** `householdId`. Otherwise `possibleDuplicate = false` and `possibleDuplicateOf` left absent. (Hard duplicates already rejected in step 8; same-household members are skipped.)\n\n## 14. `SaveOwner` (side-effect)\n- Persists the owner via `ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 generates the id.\n\n## 15. `AuditOwnerCreated` (side-effect)\n- Logs an `AUDIT` line: owner `id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, and `membershipLevel` (from `OwnerMapper.membershipLevel`). Runs after save so the id exists.\n\n## 16. `RespondWithOwnerCreated` (side-effect \u2014 response)\n- Maps to `OwnerDto` and sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the DTO body.\n\n---\n\nTwo things worth flagging since they aren't obvious from the YAML comments: **ValidateOwnerFields also rejects disposable email domains** (step 1), and the ordering choice means a **malformed body (400) is reported before capacity/limit conflicts (409/429)** \u2014 but note capacity/daily-limit checks (steps 3\u20134) run *before* duplicate checks, so a request could get a 429 even though it would also have been a 409 duplicate."
